\name{cellucid_cells_read_genes}
\alias{cellucid_cells_read_genes}
\title{Read genes for more cells}
\usage{
cellucid_cells_read_genes(viewer, cells)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{cells}{How many of the open cells; more than are open reads every one. A whole number (at least 1). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Read every gene for the first \code{cells} open cells (a dataset stored cell by cell reads genes for a sample of the open cells); stopping keeps what was read.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{cells.read-genes} (Data). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{cells}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_cells_read_genes(viewer, cells = 1)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
